feat(pivot): cross-sectional IC probe — verdict KILL

Cheapest decisive de-risk of the cross-sectional pivot axis (after all
model/backtest-side levers proved negative OOS on BTC-1m):
- quantsys/data/universe.py — PerpUniverse (top-N USDT-perp, BTC anchor)
- scripts/xs_01_download.py — 16 perps (klines+funding, BTC span)
- scripts/xs_02_panel_signals.py — existing ensemble applied per-asset
  (z->raw denormalize honored), 30-candle grid -> data/xs/mu_panel.parquet
- scripts/xs_03_ic_report.py — cross-sectional Spearman IC, non-overlapping
  OOS sub-periods, pre-registered KILL/PROCEED verdict

Result (OOS): mean cross-sectional IC +0.0138, t=1.86 (<2), 4/5 sub-periods
positive; top-bottom gross spread +1.5bps/step, net -0.00245/step (13bps/leg)
-> VERDICT KILL. The rank signal is cross-sectionally weakly positive (sign
correct, NOT anti-predictive like single-asset) but ~17x below cost: the wall
is MAGNITUDE, not sign. Portfolio layer not built (de-risk saved the M build).

Next axes saved in STATUS.md + memory pivot_fanout_2026_06_06: timeframe-1h
(attacks magnitude-vs-cost directly, recommended), vol-S (closes B2 + jump
gate), ES 1m. data/xs and results/xs are gitignored (reproducible via xs_*).

